{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>And He remembered</b> — the covenant of Abraham. But the correct interpretation in my eyes: the covenant of Sinai, for there it is written: \"and I will remember for them the covenant of the first ones,\" and they are those who came out of Egypt. And likewise it is written: \"whom I brought out,\" and He called them \"first ones,\" for they are our first fathers who received the Torah at Mount Sinai, for he has already mentioned in the passage the covenant of the three patriarchs." "<b>And He relented</b> — by way of metaphor."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 106, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:51.177376104Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}